<!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-print-guide","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-print-guide"><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-print-intro","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-print-intro"><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-breadcrumb"} --><p class="fr-breadcrumb"><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/how-to-pray-the-rosary/' ) ); ?>">Learn the Rosary</a> / Prayer guide</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {"level":1} --><h1 class="wp-block-heading">The Rosary,<br>beside you.</h1><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-lead"} --><p class="fr-lead">Every prayer. All four sets of mysteries.<br>Read here, or print a copy to share.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-print-actions"><button type="button" class="fr-primary" data-print-guide>Print this guide</button><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/how-to-pray-the-rosary/#guided-prayer' ) ); ?>">Follow the interactive Rosary</a></div><!-- /wp:html --></div><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading fr-prayer-texts","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"prayer-words-complete"} --><section id="prayer-words-complete" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading fr-prayer-texts"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Rosary prayers in English</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Begin with the Sign of the Cross, the Apostles’ Creed, one Our Father, three Hail Marys and the Glory Be. For each decade, pray one Our Father, ten Hail Marys and the Glory Be. After the five decades, pray the Hail, Holy Queen and close with the Sign of the Cross. The concluding prayer is included below, alongside the prayers for each decade.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>The Sign of the Cross</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>The Apostles’ Creed</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>I believe in God, the Father Almighty, creator of heaven and earth, and in Jesus Christ, his only Son, our Lord, who was conceived by the Holy Spirit, born of the Virgin Mary, suffered under Pontius Pilate, was crucified, died and was buried; he descended into hell; on the third day he rose again from the dead; he ascended into heaven, and is seated at the right hand of God the Father Almighty; from there he will come again to judge the living and the dead. I believe in the Holy Spirit, the holy catholic Church, the communion of saints, the forgiveness of sins, the resurrection of the body, and life everlasting. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>Our Father</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name; thy kingdom come; thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread; and forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us; and lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>Hail Mary</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee. Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus. Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>Glory Be</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit. As it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>Hail, Holy Queen</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Hail, Holy Queen, Mother of Mercy, our life, our sweetness, and our hope. To thee do we cry, poor banished children of Eve: to thee do we send up our sighs, mourning and weeping in this valley of tears. Turn then, O most gracious Advocate, thine eyes of mercy toward us, and after this, our exile, show unto us the blessed fruit of thy womb, Jesus. O clement, O loving, O sweet Virgin Mary! Pray for us, O Holy Mother of God, that we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:details {"showContent":true} --><details class="wp-block-details" open><summary>Concluding prayer</summary><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>O God, whose only begotten Son, by His life, death and Resurrection, has purchased for us the rewards of eternal life; grant, we beseech Thee, that by meditating upon these Mysteries of the Most Holy Rosary of the Blessed Virgin Mary, we may imitate what they contain and obtain what they promise, through the same Christ our Lord. Amen.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></details><!-- /wp:details --><!-- wp:paragraph {"className":"fr-source-note"} --><p class="fr-source-note">Prayer texts reproduced from <a class="text-link" href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Family Rosary’s existing guide</a>.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading","layout":{"type":"default"},"tagName":"section","anchor":"mysteries"} --><section id="mysteries" class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-section fr-reading"><!-- wp:heading {"level":2} --><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Mysteries of the Rosary by day</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>The days below follow a common weekly pattern. Sunday customs can vary with the liturgical season; you may choose another set.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:html --><div class="fr-mystery-list"><details open><summary>Joyful mysteries <span>Monday and Saturday</span></summary><ol><li>The Annunciation</li><li>The Visitation</li><li>The Nativity</li><li>The Presentation</li><li>The Finding of Jesus in the Temple</li></ol></details><details open><summary>Sorrowful mysteries <span>Tuesday and Friday</span></summary><ol><li>The Agony in the Garden</li><li>The Scourging at the Pillar</li><li>The Crowning with Thorns</li><li>The Carrying of the Cross</li><li>The Crucifixion</li></ol></details><details open><summary>Glorious mysteries <span>Wednesday and Sunday</span></summary><ol><li>The Resurrection</li><li>The Ascension</li><li>The Descent of the Holy Spirit</li><li>The Assumption</li><li>The Coronation of Mary</li></ol></details><details open><summary>Luminous mysteries <span>Thursday</span></summary><ol><li>The Baptism of Jesus</li><li>The Wedding at Cana</li><li>The Proclamation of the Kingdom</li><li>The Transfiguration</li><li>The Institution of the Eucharist</li></ol></details></div><!-- /wp:html --></section><!-- /wp:group --><!-- wp:group {"className":"fr-wrap fr-reading fr-print-source","layout":{"type":"default"}} --><div class="wp-block-group fr-wrap fr-reading fr-print-source"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Prayer order and mystery reference: <a href="https://www.usccb.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">USCCB</a>. Prayer words: <a href="https://www.familyrosary.org/how-to-pray-the-rosary">Family Rosary’s existing guide</a>. Spanish and Portuguese guides are also available from that page.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:group -->